WEBVTT

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:58.530
This season, we begin

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.610
Cosplay Contest

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:35.490
Pastimers
Club

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.200
We finally got permission to show a movie for the cultural festival!

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.850
So what do we have left to do?

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.810
We'll need to put together a theater in here.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:42.840
I wanna do some behind the scenes stuff too!

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.830
We can show off costumes and put up displays of production stuff.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.620
Costumes, huh?

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.750
Olivia-san, what do you think about the costume from the movie?

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.520
The sexy spy outfit?

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.760
Hell no! I never want to wear that skintight thing again.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:55.870
I refuse!

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.300
Then what <i>do</i> you wanna wear?

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.560
I mean, it's kind of a cliché...

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.430
but, a maid, maybe?

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:03.350
Like in a café?

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:03.930
Like this?

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:05.350
Like this?

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:05.350
Uh, no.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.940
I mean like in olden times.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.760
I like it! You'd look great!

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:13.360
I'd love to see you carry a basket bag.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:16.280
Is there any kind of outfit you want to try out, Hanako-san?

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.810
Me? If we're talking movies, it's gotta be denim!

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:24.580
So I wanna try the popular denim-on-denim look!

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:28.670
<i>Wait, what? Hanako's train of thought sometimes has a serious missing link.</i>

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:31.920
Are there any popular movies with a denim-on-denim outfit?

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:32.750
Knock, knock!

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:35.690
Hel-<i>lo</i>? Anyone in there?

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:36.380
Jesus.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.200
It makes you want to back up to the future.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.580
Yeah, it really does!

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:40.930
What's that supposed to mean?

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.290
What about you, Kasumi-san?

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.440
Who, me? Um...

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:45.800
Let me think...

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:48.390
A simple costume you might find in a movie...

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.650
A s-sailor suit, then.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:52.690
With a big gun?

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:53.570
Or a samurai sword?

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:55.080
There are a lot of options.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.360
Lemme get a bunch of them ready.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.300
Hey, Maeda?

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.000
<i>She's handy.</i>

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.780
<i>Hanako-san's a handy girl to have around.</i>

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.370
<i>And then what happened?</i>

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.000
I'm terribly sorry for the delay.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.370
I was unable to obtain permission
to bring weaponry through security,

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:12.000
so I was forced to enter by alternative means.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.120
Yippee!

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.880
<i>Tell me they're not real...</i>

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.010
We're gonna get changed, so go kill some time outside somewhere, Maeda.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.340
As you wish.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:20.150
Okay!

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:22.550
Let's start the costume parade!

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.390
First up: Olivia!

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.390
H-How do I look?

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.720
You're adorable!

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.730
Salutations from Downton Abbey!

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.660
Do my hair, Olivia.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.400
Certainly, young miss!

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.940
Your hair is so silky smooth!

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:40.710
Style my hair super splendidly for my upcoming marriage meeting.

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:42.030
<i>That was fun to say.</i>

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.660
What do you think?

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.260
You're fired.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.780
Don't bother coming in tomorrow.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.610
Wh-What? Can I put you down as a reference?

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:49.620
Forget it.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.420
Now I'm jobless!

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:53.340
I worked so hard!

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.280
My turn! I counter Olivia-san!

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.210
Only Shadow-Game-obsessed card gamers
with split personalities would wear this hairstyle!

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.950
Let's move on to Kasumi-san.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.090
O-Okay.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:07.600
H-How do I look?

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.770
Lookin' good! Now try singing!

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:15.860
How I long to hold you...

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.860
<i>Kasumi can't carry a tune, huh...
Hey, when did everything get so weird?</i>

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:17.610
That sailor suit looks totally cute on you!

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.440
I'm glad. I always wanted to try it.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:21.610
Now you, Hanako.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:24.240
Now the star of the show!

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.280
<i>Is she supposed to be a Vietnam War protester?</i>

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.660
Huh? Isn't that the wrong reaction?

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:34.390
No, I'm pretty sure it's not.

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:35.330
It's not?!

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.980
You know what? It's probably the hair.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:38.750
I seriously doubt that.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.760
I know I can't really talk,
but you look way out of style.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.720
No way! I thought denim-on-denim was a popular look!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.680
Um... Can I ask where you got those?

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:53.720
I wanted the denim secondhand,
so I had Maeda buy some overseas for me!

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.050
Doesn't it look authentic?

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:58.020
Oh, I was <i>wondering</i> about the bloodstained hole.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:02.290
I wonder if it's because denim's supposed to look worn.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.030
<i>Wait, it's already secondhand, so...</i>

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.910
Ah, I gotcha.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:08.490
I'll go for the ripped-up look.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.990
That'll do it.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:16.400
Um... why did you do <i>vertical</i> cuts?

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:19.000
It looks like you got attacked by a slasher.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:19.840
No good?

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.400
You usually go horizontal.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.100
U-sual-ly?

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.860
Who's in charge of what "usual" is?

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:26.290
Who's in charge of what "common sense" is?

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:28.140
You're missing the point.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:32.240
The idea is that, due to the fabric's construction, the warp on the surface wears over time

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:35.500
and exposes the weft underneath.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.150
But when you cut it vertically, you destroyed the whole weave.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.970
Seriously? Well, what do I do?

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:41.480
That's what <i>I</i> want to ask.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:43.970
And now you're bleeding, since you cut the skin too.

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:46.820
Who the hell would cut clothes while she's still wearing them?

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:52.660
But now you look like you've been dragged through battle and come out bloodied and beaten all over.

00:05:53.570 --> 00:05:54.770
Congratulations.

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.600
Congratulations.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:05:59.920
Thank you.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.740
Wait, shit! I was just about to go through Instrumentality!

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:04.270
Thanks for helping set up the gag.

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:06.140
What am I gonna <i>do</i>?!

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:09.100
Um... what about if you hold the rifle?

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:13.220
<i>I look like I'm about to kill some zombies.</i>

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:16.440
It... looks like a movie parody now?
So I guess it works.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.440
Really? You mean it?

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:20.210
Well, we still need to get approval for the costumes.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:21.670
Okay! Let's do it!

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:23.580
Wait, while we're still wearing them?

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:25.570
Seeing's believing, ya know!

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:27.240
I guess so.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:28.070
Yes.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.330
Student Council Room

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:33.990
Huh?

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:35.540
Who could that be?

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:36.500
I'll go an' check!

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.170
Hey there! What can I do you fo—

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:43.380
Prez! The Pastimers Club are back to settle the score!

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.620
What? No, no! We're here to apply for—

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:47.280
What do you demand this time?

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:50.030
We won't give in to you savages!

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:52.220
No, no! Just <i>listen</i>!

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.010
<i>Asobi Asobase!</i>

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:57.520
To the Future Me

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.810
What are you all doing over summer vacation?

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:00.590
What should I do?

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:02.730
Sleep in 'til midday, then hang out with Toshio...

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.860
But you always hang out with Toshio-kun.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.830
But I don't always sleep in 'til midday.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:08.400
We're gonna see a movie too.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:09.820
Really? Another horror movie?

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:10.610
<i>Titanic</i>.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.120
You haven't seen it? It's almost out of theaters.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.580
Nah, I'm seeing it for the fifth time.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.790
Chii-chan! Let's do the thing from <i>Titanic</i>!

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:18.580
Oh, that thing. Yeah, let's do it!

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.830
All right. Open your eyes.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.340
I'm flying!

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:26.450
Oh geez!

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:28.210
Jack...

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:36.510
You really love your pro wrestling.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:41.480
You bet! I'm thinking of applying for AJW when I graduate!

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:45.230
Oh. It's Toshio.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.570
Ooh! What does he want?

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:48.920
Let's go to Shibuya.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.110
Let's go to Shibuya.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.290
Shibuya, huh?

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:53.900
It's such a pain, carrying a pager and a phone around.

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:56.240
When will he give up the pager already?

00:07:56.240 --> 00:08:00.370
That's the latest model PHS phone! It's so cool!

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.600
My daddy bought it for me.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.040
Your <i>sugar</i> daddy?

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.520
Oh yeah, my senpai from the Pro Wrestling Club
did this joke with one of those!

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:08.050
Really? Show me, show me.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.730
Oh no, I can't get signal.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:14.470
Let me extend the antenna. No signal. No signal.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.550
Piece of shit!

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:17.330
That's how it goes.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.660
<i>Was that meant to be a joke?</i>

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:23.200
What do I do? There's... no signal.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.730
Hey, there was no signal anyway,
so don't worry about it.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:26.790
By the way, this thing...

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:28.110
Oh yeah.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.730
I said I wanted a computer for the clubroom,
so my dad gave me this!

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:34.820
Wow! Can it do that Windows thing?

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:38.080
Dunno. He said it was a Mac-in-tosh or something.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:41.380
Hold on. Why did we make this club again?

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.790
The Film Club?

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:45.420
Well, Umeko quit the basketball club,

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:49.550
and the school rules say you need to join one,
so she made her own.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:52.260
That's it. God, I hate school clubs.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.750
What kind of project should we do for the culture festival?

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:56.220
Make a movie?

00:08:56.220 --> 00:09:00.850
Hm... could we do a documentary on your pro wrestling fanclub, Hijiri?

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:01.440
Sure.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:05.350
You keep being so obsessed with pro wrestling and you'll lose your chance to get a boyfriend.

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:07.400
Whatever. It's not like I'll get married.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:08.330
You won't?

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:08.830
Nope.

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:10.860
Huh. And you're so popular, too.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:13.110
Well, like...

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:16.080
If I have to look after a husband and kids,

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:18.740
I might lose my mind.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:22.880
Really? I wanna get married at 25
and have a baby at 27!

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:25.170
I could look after them fine!

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:26.090
That's so you.

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:29.130
Though there are more men getting domestic nowadays.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.490
I'm planning to get married at 22.

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:33.420
I can see that.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.720
I wonder how we'll all end up at 30.

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:39.430
Let's write messages in the computer—
like a time capsule.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.230
We'll read them in 15 years' time.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:43.800
Will this computer still be here in 15 years?

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:46.050
Of course it will. It's the latest model.

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:49.150
It'll be ages before there's anything newer.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:50.270
I guess you're right.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:51.320
Yep!

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:53.610
I'll boot it up.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.030
Wanna play cards?

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.280
Let's play Sevens.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.220
So bored...

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:05.080
Hey, it's booted.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.580
Sure took a while.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.040
Does this work?

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:08.960
Yes!

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.900
To me at age 30:

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:15.710
Are you living it up overseas

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:19.720
after marrying an oil baron and becoming a multi-millionaire?

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:22.240
To me at age 30:

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:28.530
Are you living a life of domestic bliss

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:33.610
after meeting Prince Charming at around age 25 and having two children?

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.940
To me at age 30:

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:38.840
Did you become the second Crush Gals?

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:42.370
You should be world champion by now, right?

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:48.910
Writing a letter to our 30-year-old selves using a computer feels like something out of a sci-fi movie.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.580
Let's meet up here when we all turn 30!

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:52.130
Okay!

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.000
I hope the computer's still here.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.820
Of course it will be!

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.720
Pastimers
Club

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.140
How's motherhood treating you?

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:07.440
It's not easy, but it's fun.

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:09.770
I can't believe Hijiri's the only one of us who got married.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:13.150
Something about the craziest one landing a husband ticks me off.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.360
Don't be mean!

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:15.600
Can I touch him?

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:16.360
Go ahead.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:19.700
Your nail!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:22.200
C-Calm down! It's a fake nail! A fake nail, okay?

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.560
Sorry about that. He's a little shy with new people.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:27.300
Though I think he got along with the girls in Chii-chan's club.

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:28.250
Wanna try again?

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.060
No thanks.

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:30.960
He looks like he's gunning for my real nail.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:34.080
Raising a baby seems like a lot of work.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.820
And a husband on top...

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.190
Frankly, I'm impressed.

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:38.340
It all worked out.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:41.370
By the way, what about that computer?

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:44.380
They'd already thrown it out when I started working here.

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:47.730
What did we write back then again?

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:49.040
I forget.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.890
<i>Asobi Asobase!</i>
